{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GAZG4WgtzLPpudo8cHe1wm","type":"tool_result","content":"package config\n\n// SelectReviewers returns the reviewer roles that review a PR by default, in\n// config order. The candidates are worker.Reviewers (only roles that exist)\n// when it is non-empty, else every reviewer role; a candidate stays when its\n// When matches. A worker's list narrows the candidates and never bypasses\n// when:. Lead or worker next requests are added by the caller.\nfunc (r *Resolved) SelectReviewers(worker Role, changed []string, triageRan func(string) bool) []string {\n\tvar allowed map[string]bool\n\tif len(worker.Reviewers) > 0 {\n\t\tallowed = map[string]bool{}\n\t\tfor _, n := range worker.Reviewers {\n\t\t\tallowed[n] = true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tvar out []string\n\tfor _, role := range r.RolesOf(KindReviewer) {\n\t\tif allowed != nil && !allowed[role.Name] {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif role.When.Matches(changed, triageRan) {\n\t\t\tout = append(out, role.Name)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn out\n}\n--- a/internal/closeout/closeout.go\n+++ b/internal/closeout/closeout.go\n+\n+// TriageRoles returns the triage roles that ran to a closed, done close-out\n+// for issue. Failed, open and needs-human jobs do not count.\n+func TriageRoles(ctx context.Context, s interface {\n+\tCloseoutsOf(ctx context.Context, issue int, stage string) ([]state.Job, error)\n+}, issue int) (map[string]bool, error) {\n+\tjobs, err := s.CloseoutsOf(ctx, issue, StageTriage)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"triage roles of issue %d: %w\", issue, err)\n+\t}\n+\tout := map[string]bool{}\n+\tfor _, sj := range jobs {\n+\t\trec, err := decode(sj)\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn nil, err\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif rec.Phase == PhaseClosed && rec.Plan.Outcome == OutcomeDone {\n+\t\t\tout[sj.Role] = true\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn out, nil\n+}\n--- a/internal/config/types.go\n+++ b/internal/config/types.go\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/bmatcuk/doublestar/v4\"\n-// Semantics are owned by #15; config only validates and exposes the shape.\n+// See Matches for the semantics.\n+\n+// Matches reports whether the reviewer runs: a nil When always does;\n+// otherwise it does when any changed path matches any Paths entry, or any\n+// Triage role has run (triageRan). Matching is case-sensitive and anchored at\n+// the repo root. An entry ending in \"/\" is a directory, matched on a segment\n+// boundary; any other entry is a doublestar glob where \"*\" stays within a\n+// segment and \"**\" crosses them (\"**/go.mod\" matches a root go.mod, while a\n+// slash-free glob such as \"go.mod\" matches only at the root). A nil changed\n+// means the changed paths are unknown: a rule with Paths then matches (fail\n+// open); an empty non-nil slice means nothing changed.\n+func (w *When) Matches(changed []string, triageRan func(role string) bool) bool {\n+\tif w == nil {\n+\t\treturn true\n+\t}\n+\tif changed == nil && len(w.Paths) > 0 {\n+\t\treturn true\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, e := range w.Paths {\n+\t\tfor _, p := range changed {\n+\t\t\tif matchWhen(e, p) {\n+\t\t\t\treturn true\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif triageRan != nil {\n+\t\tfor _, t := range w.Triage {\n+\t\t\tif triageRan(t) {\n+\t\t\t\treturn true\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn false\n+}\n+\n+func matchWhen(entry, p string) bool {\n+\tif strings.HasSuffix(entry, \"/\") {\n+\t\treturn strings.HasPrefix(p, entry) || p == strings.TrimSuffix(entry, \"/\")\n+\t}\n+\tm, err := doublestar.Match(entry, p)\n+\treturn err == nil && m\n+}\n--- a/internal/gitx/local.go\n+++ b/internal/gitx/local.go\n+// Renames are not detected: a rename lists both the old and the new path, and\n+// a deletion is listed.\n-\targs := append([]string{\"--literal-pathspecs\", \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"-z\", from, to, \"--\"}, paths...)\n+\targs := append([]string{\"--literal-pathspecs\", \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--no-renames\", \"-z\", from, to, \"--\"}, paths...)\n--- a/internal/worker/run.go\n+++ b/internal/worker/run.go\n+\thead     string // the latest commit pushed (or the base when nothing was)\n+\t\tjb.head = s.h.BaseSHA\n+\tjb.head = res.SHA\n-// reviewers lists the reviewer roles to request on the PR: the role's\n-// reviewers, or every reviewer role when none are set, then the reviewers\n-// triage deferred; only roles that exist, without duplicates.\n+// reviewers lists the reviewer roles to request on the PR. The base set is\n+// config's SelectReviewers: the role's reviewers (or every reviewer role)\n+// whose when: rule matches the PR's changed paths (merge base to head) or the\n+// triage roles that ran (closed done, or labelled done). Reviewers triage\n+// deferred are then added unconditionally; the worker's own next requests are\n+// added by close-out. Selection is monotonic: every run recomputes from the\n+// whole PR diff and close-out only adds labels, so earlier requests stay and\n+// newly matching reviewers are added. When the head is unknown or git fails,\n+// path rules fail open. Only roles that exist, without duplicates.\n-\tvar names []string\n-\tif len(jb.role.Reviewers) > 0 {\n-\t\tnames = append(names, jb.role.Reviewers...)\n-\t} else {\n-\t\tfor _, r := range jb.cfg.RolesOf(config.KindReviewer) {\n-\t\t\tnames = append(names, r.Name)\n+\tchanged := jb.changedPaths(ctx)\n+\tran := map[string]bool{}\n+\ttr, err := closeout.TriageRoles(ctx, jb.l.d.Store, jb.is.Number)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tjb.log.Warn(\"worker.reviewers_failed\", \"step\", \"triage\", \"error\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor k := range tr {\n+\t\tran[k] = true\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, r := range jb.cfg.RolesOf(config.KindTriage) {\n+\t\tfor _, l := range jb.is.Labels {\n+\t\t\tif l == labels.Done(labels.StageTriage, r.Name) {\n+\t\t\t\tran[r.Name] = true\n+\t\t\t}\n+\tnames := jb.cfg.SelectReviewers(jb.role, changed, func(r string) bool { return ran[r] })\n+\tif len(out) == 0 && len(jb.cfg.RolesOf(config.KindReviewer)) > 0 {\n+\t\tjb.log.Warn(\"worker.no_reviewers\", \"issue\", jb.is.Number, \"branch\", jb.branch)\n+\t}\n+\treturn out\n+}\n+\n+// changedPaths lists the paths the PR changes (merge base of the config\n+// commit and head, to head) without the .ard/ and .ard-input/ trees. A nil\n+// result means the paths are unknown: path rules then fail open.\n+func (jb *job) changedPaths(ctx context.Context) []string {\n+\tif jb.head == \"\" || strings.Trim(jb.head, \"0\") == \"\" {\n+\t\treturn nil\n+\t}\n+\tg, dir := jb.l.d.Git, jb.l.d.RepoDir\n+\tbase, err := g.MergeBase(ctx, dir, jb.cfg.SHA, jb.head)\n+\tstep := \"merge_base\"\n+\tvar ps []string\n+\tif err == nil {\n+\t\tstep = \"changed_paths\"\n+\t\tps, err = g.ChangedPaths(ctx, dir, base, jb.head)\n+\t}\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tjb.log.Warn(\"worker.reviewers_failed\", \"step\", step, \"error\", err)\n+\t\treturn nil\n+\t}\n+\tout := []string{}\n+\tfor _, p := range ps {\n+\t\tif p == \".ard\" || p == \".ard-input\" || strings.HasPrefix(p, \".ard/\") || strings.HasPrefix(p, \".ard-input/\") {\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tout = append(out, p)\n+\t}\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nEvaluates reviewer `when:` rules when a worker opens or updates its PR, so path- or triage-gated reviewers run only when they apply, instead of every reviewer always running.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/config`: `When.Matches` (paths OR triage; case-sensitive, root-anchored; `dir/` prefixes, doublestar globs; unknown paths fail open) and `Resolved.SelectReviewers` (a worker's `reviewers:` narrows candidates, `when:` still decides). Loading now keeps a trailing `/` and validates globs in `when.paths`, and rejects a `when:` with neither paths nor triage.\n- `internal/closeout`: `TriageRoles` returns triage roles with a closed `done` close-out only (needs-human does not count).\n- `internal/gitx`: `ChangedPaths` uses `--no-renames`, so renames list both paths and deletions appear.\n- `internal/worker`: the job records the pushed head; `reviewers` diffs merge base to head (dropping `.ard/` and `.ard-input/`), selects via config, then adds lead-deferred requests unconditionally. A git failure fails open for path rules and logs `worker.reviewers_failed`. An empty selection logs `worker.no_reviewers`; the PR stays a draft. The `Git` interface gains `ChangedPaths`. Worker `next` reviews are still added by close-out.\n- `internal/configcmd`: `config check` warns when every reviewer has a `when:`.\n- `docs/proposal.md`: documents the rules, the warning and the starter example.\n\n## Testing\n`make test` passes (all packages). Added tests: load (dir slash, invalid glob, empty `when`), `Matches` table, `SelectReviewers`, `ChangedPaths` renames/deletions, `TriageRoles`, config check warning, and worker tests for path hit/miss, triage label, running triage not counting, worker list narrowing without bypassing `when:`, `.ard/` not selectable, and fail-open on a git error.\n\n## Open issues\n- Not tested at worker level: lead-deferred bypass, store-error fallback to labels, the monotonic two-run case and the `worker.no_reviewers` log line; the logic is simple, but those plan test-plan items are missing.\n- `internal/roles/config.yaml` had no `when:` text to update, so I left it alone.\n- Process note: I ran `git checkout -- internal/closeout/closeout.go` once to undo my own accidental overwrite of that file; no ref or HEAD changed.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"109f3186-a1d7-435d-9cc0-73031ff9468b","uuid":"7e2fa9d9-b8d0-45f0-aace-2df29d9b6a54","timestamp":"2026-11-23T15:44:46.487Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"package config\n\n// SelectReviewers returns the reviewer roles that review a PR by default, in\n// config order. The candidates are worker.Reviewers (only roles that exist)\n// when it is non-empty, else every reviewer role; a candidate stays when its\n// When matches. A worker's list narrows the candidates and never bypasses\n// when:. Lead or worker next requests are added by the caller.\nfunc (r *Res